Change when `PATCH` notifications are sent, and allow a Review Stage
alongside another partial Stage, in apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml

Generated on 2026-11-26, against the swagger.yaml committed in 854c9e2.
Apply from the repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/api-patch-006-notifications-review-stage.patch

These come from the user's decisions on 2026-11-26, made while drawing
`data-sync-sequence.md` from the data-sync slide (DSYNC p1):

1. `PATCH …/stages/{stageid}` (`updateStage`): a notification is sent
   when another organisation's partial Stage is new to the caller, or has
   been saved since the caller was last told about it. Before, one was
   sent on every save while another organisation had a partial Stage
   open, and edits weren't reported. The user chose this over notifying
   only on changes since the caller's own last save, which would never
   report an idle Stage last saved before the caller started theirs.
2. `POST …/stages` (`createStage`): an exception to one partial Stage per
   organisation (User 2026-11-23 Q28). A Stage of the Review type may be
   opened alongside the organisation's partial Stage while it takes in
   another organisation's completed Stage. This matches the slide, where
   the "System holds both open Stages". ⚠️ The limits (one Review Stage
   at a time, only while a Stage is still to be taken in) are inferred,
   and whether the type is always Review is open (Q27, for YJB).

